WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.337
- Well today is emlocated.

00:00:01.337 --> 00:00:04.690
So, what does his legacy
mean to you specifically?

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:05.600
- It's, wow.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.330
I mean that's, it's, there's so much,

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:08.590
I couldn't even begin to cover it,

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:11.110
but just all his activism
and everything that,

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.127
he did in the civil war for
the civil rights movement.

00:00:13.127 --> 00:00:13.960
- Selflessness.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:16.950
- Selflessness and, just
the human being that he was.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.870
And I'll always respect
everything that he's done,

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:21.260
but in particular, how he did it,

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:24.120
he just uses articulations
and his knowledge

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.200
and his charisma, as power.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.440
And I love that.
- Which is true power.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:29.760
- He knew it was very effective.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:31.485
It's true power and it was very effective.

00:00:31.485 --> 00:00:34.330
And, I just truly, I
mean, I can't say enough.

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:35.670
I mean, we can go on for
this about five minutes.

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:38.740
- I know that's hard to wrap
it up in a synopsis, yeah.

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:39.720
I would never have asked the question.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.650
- But no, it's everything
that he stands for.

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:43.483
And even unfortunately,

00:00:43.483 --> 00:00:44.961
even if we listened to a speech today,

00:00:44.961 --> 00:00:46.924
we,
- Still relevant.

00:00:46.924 --> 00:00:49.070
- Still relevant, still relevant.

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:51.030
We still have a ways to go.

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:51.872
- Amen.

00:00:51.872 --> 00:00:52.705
(audience clapping)

00:00:52.705 --> 00:00:53.538
Well, you, you visited the motel

00:00:53.538 --> 00:00:54.700
where Dr. King was assassinated.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:55.930
Was that-
- Yes.

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:57.363
- what was that like for you?

00:00:57.363 --> 00:01:00.730
- I was there and I said, oh yeah,

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:02.810
I wanna go by there, just to be there

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:07.810
and just to look at the layout
of everything from afar and-

00:01:08.218 --> 00:01:09.410
- It had to feel intense.

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:10.420
- It was definitely intense.

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:12.300
It was definitely intense
to know that he was there

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.760
and everything that's happened there.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:16.490
And it was just something
that I just had to see.

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:17.650
And I was glad that I was there.

00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:18.650
I was glad that I saw it

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:20.710
and I took a picture of it, of course.

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:22.350
And, I have it up on my wall.

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:24.309
And it's just one of those things to wear,

00:01:24.309 --> 00:01:26.270
it's just a moment in time,

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:28.330
to know that I was there where such,

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:33.330
a powerful, effective person
was and, it's very powerful.

